From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Otto=20Pfl=C3=BCger?= <otto.pflueger@abscue.de>
Date: Sat, 1 Mar 2025 16:14:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 080/225] rpmsg: add driver for Unisoc SIPC
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add an rpmsg backend implementing the SIPC protocol used for
communication with various remote processors found on Unisoc SoCs. SIPC
supports both packet-based ("sblock") and serial ("sbuf") channels.
Each "sbuf" channel consists of multiple buffers that can be used for
separate data streams, whereas each "sblock" channel only provides a
single endpoint for sending and receiving data. Additionally, a system
known as "sipx", currently only used for modem network interfaces,
provides sblock-like channels with a shared buffer pool and support for
a secondary endpoint for ACK packets.

There are some additional special-purpose channel types which are
not implemented in this driver yet.

Since the remote processors only provide channel numbers and no other
information, use the device tree to get type definitions and
human-readable names for the channels.

Signed-off-by: Otto Pflüger <otto.pflueger@abscue.de>
